<title>DUBAI: Saudi sends $2.6 million in aid to Palestinians.</title>
<headline>Saudi sends $2.6 million in aid to Palestinians.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-11-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia sent on Sunday 9.5 million riyals ($2.6 million) in aid to the Palestinian Authority, the official Saudi Press Agency (SPA) reported.</p>
<p>It said the move was ordered by Prince Salman, the governor of Riyadh.</p>
<p>Saudi Arabia and other Gulf states were major financial contributors to the Palestine Liberation Organisation (PLO) before they severed aid in anger at Palestinian sympathy for Iraq during the Gulf War.</p>
<p>Saudi-PLO ties have improved over the years.</p>
</text>
